WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.540
Some superhero cartoons have multiple seasons
to tell their story, while others end abruptly,

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.160
often on cliffhangers, left eternally unresolved.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.740
Here are the real reasons these animated superhero
shows were canceled, although in many cases,

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.029
knowing why won't make their absence any easier.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:22.540
Virgil Hawkins is that most classic of superheroes
a normal kid until he suddenly very much isn't.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:27.609
Transformed by exposure to a mutagen gas,
he gains the ability to control electromagnetism

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:30.570
and becomes Static, hero of Dakota City.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.790
And alongside his best friend, Richie, he
spent four seasons of Static Shock battling

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:39.320
bad guys, learning life lessons, and occasionally
hanging out with Shaquille O'Neal.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.940
"What's up, little man?

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.940
You must be-"

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:42.940
"Shaq."

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.150
"No, I'm Shaq.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.150
You gotta be Virgil.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.200
I've heard a lot about you."

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.790
Fans flocked to it.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.220
Static Shock earned high ratings from the
very beginning, to the point of surpassing

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.860
all other kids' shows save global juggernaut
Pokemon.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.790
Nor did these ratings slacken with time.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.070
Reruns aired on Cartoon Network outstripped
all other children's programming.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.070
What, then, put a halt to Static's crackling
popularity?

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.470
Well, it was something that had nothing to
do with ratings: merchandising.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:11.760
As creator Dwayne McDuffie recounted years
after the show's end, animation is enormously

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.220
expensive to produce, and it depends upon
the success of multiple revenue streams.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:22.100
A well-rated cartoon must also have profitable
toys, T-shirts, video games, and tie-in books,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.570
which Static Shock lacked.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:27.140
Sadly, toy companies weren't as keen on the
cartoon as kids were.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.180
McDuffie explained to The World's Finest:

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:34.380
"After five years, we had a Subway value meal,
two Scholastic book adaptations, one DVD,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.159
and a Gameboy Advance game."

00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:40.800
Being able to do as many episodes as they
did was, quote, "a gift" one that fans the

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.700
world over were ecstatic to receive.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.310
Teen Titans' slick style, unforgettable theme
song, and clever twists on superheroic tropes

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.479
dazzled fans right off the bat.

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:54.729
Created to appeal to younger viewers, it was
goofy, though nowhere near the levels of its

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:59.400
successor, Teen Titans Go!, approachable to
comics newbies, and with its anime-inspired

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.190
aesthetic, it was unlike any other superhero
cartoon then on the air.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:08.810
Though the series' final episode aired in
January 2006, fan campaigns to resurrect Teen

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.060
Titans continue to thrive online.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.250
Their passion is real...yet so is the series'
demise.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.940
"As long as we're still here, we still have
a chance.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:18.640
And that's why we're going to keep fighting."

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.160
What stopped Robin and his merry band of adolescent
avengers?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.319
A variety of explanations have been offered
over the years.

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:28.810
Wil Wheaton, voice of Aqualad, asserts that
Warner Brothers executives were unimpressed

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.819
by the sixth season's pitch.

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:34.730
Story editor Rob Hoegee, however, has gone
on record as saying that it was a decision

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.530
made by Cartoon Network instead of Warner
Brothers, and that the crew knew that the

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.650
fifth season would be the show's last.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:45.010
Producer and writer David Slack has suggested
two additional reasons as to why the show

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.010
ended.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.780
First, it might've been because ratings dropped
after Teen Titans' dark fourth season, or

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.709
it might've been thanks to a dispute over
toy licensing.

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:56.530
As Bandai had the show's toy deal and Cartoon
Network switched entirely to working with

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.260
Mattel in 2006, that theory, at least, has
some degree of evidence behind it.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:06.010
No one reason for the Titans' demise may ever
emerge, yet their end remains resolutely in

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:09.340
place, much to the frustration of long-time
fans.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:14.430
Released in 2013, Beware the Batman is unique
within the Caped Crusader's animated history.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:19.459
Rendered in sleek CGI, Beware's Batman fights
alongside a significantly more spry Alfred

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:25.120
and Katana here imagined to be Alfred's goddaughter
against lesser-known Bat-baddies like Anarky,

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.849
Professor Pyg, Magpie, and Phosphorus Rex.

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:31.150
A shake-up to be sure, but one built on a
solid foundation.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.840
As series producers Glen Murakami and Mitch
Watson explained, Beware the Batman was meant

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.230
to be a return to the character's roots as
a detective.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:43.290
It had potential, talent, and vision, and
yet it was pulled from Cartoon Network's schedule

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.570
a mere three months after its premiere.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:49.860
An official explanation wasn't offered, and
the series was moved to Adult Swim's Toonami

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:50.860
block.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.840
There it stayed, until the only thing resembling
an announcement was made by Toonami's official

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:55.840
Tumblr blog:

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.290
"Bad news: We JUST (like, hours ago) found
out from our legal department that Beware

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:03.830
the Batman...[is] being 'written off,' financially,
as of now."

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:08.480
Toonami aired the final seven episodes of
the series on September 28, 2013, and that

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.480
was that.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:14.130
Other than that brief mention of financial
failure, no further explanation has arrived,

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:18.379
reruns are rare, and Batman fans must get
their animated fix via Justice League Action

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:20.590
and DC's slate of direct-to-video films.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:25.169
Beware the Batman is well on its way to becoming
much like its titular hero: a half-remembered

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:29.400
phantom, shrouded in mystery, hearsay, and
rumor.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.509
Young Justice delighted fans the world over
when, years after its 2013 cancellation, it

00:04:34.509 --> 00:04:37.389
returned for a third season, Young Justice:
Outsiders.

00:04:37.389 --> 00:04:39.419
But why was it cancelled in the first place?

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:42.939
One explanation came from Kevin Smith's Fat
Man on Batman podcast.

00:04:42.939 --> 00:04:47.999
In conversation with animation legend Paul
Dini, the two men claimed that network executives

00:04:47.999 --> 00:04:52.249
were unsatisfied with Young Justice's high
female viewership, as, quote, "they don't

00:04:52.249 --> 00:04:53.249
buy toys."

00:04:53.249 --> 00:04:56.229
Series developer Greg Weisman denied this,
however.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:05:01.080
Three years after the show's untimely end,
he identified Young Justices' weak toy sales,

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.659
unrelated to gender, as the cancellation culprit.

00:05:03.659 --> 00:05:07.219
"Well now, you're everything I like best in
a woman.

00:05:07.219 --> 00:05:08.219
An easy target."

00:05:08.219 --> 00:05:12.050
Crowdfunding efforts sprung up in the wake
of the show's cancellation, but Warner Brothers

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:16.090
made it clear that they weren't interested
in furthering Young Justice in that way.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.719
Yet somehow, things changed.

00:05:17.719 --> 00:05:22.180
Young Justice's arrival on Netflix stirred
up enough attention that rumors began to circulate

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:26.009
about a possible continuation rumors that
Weisman eventually legitimized.

00:05:26.009 --> 00:05:30.849
He urged fans to keep making noise, and eventually,
it was enough, and Young Justice returned

00:05:30.849 --> 00:05:31.849
to its eager fanbase.

00:05:31.849 --> 00:05:36.780
For some fans, dreams do come true...if your
Netflix debut produces big enough numbers,

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:37.780
anyway.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.949
Consisting of just 13 episodes, Spider-Man
Unlimited was canceled before it managed to

00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:43.569
air even half of its modest run.

00:05:43.569 --> 00:05:46.559
It wasn't miserable to look at, nor were its
ratings poor.

00:05:46.559 --> 00:05:47.559
What slew this spider?

00:05:47.559 --> 00:05:49.689
A few different things, as it turns out.

00:05:49.689 --> 00:05:51.909
To begin with, the premise was strange.

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:56.129
This cartoon follows a Peter Parker stranded
on "Counter-Earth," where he fights alongside

00:05:56.129 --> 00:06:00.449
J. Jonah Jameson's son against the forces
of the High Evolutionary.

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:04.960
Marvel wasn't pleased with this complex plotting,
but in fairness, the cartoon was looking far

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.990
afield of traditional Spider-Man stories because
it had to.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.860
"Something funny is going on here.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.879
My spider-sense is going full blast!"

00:06:12.879 --> 00:06:16.990
Spider-Man Unlimited was made by Saban Entertainment,
who had, in the wake of Sony and Marvel's

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:21.680
deal to produce Sam Raimi's Spider-Man film,
been cut off from using Spider-Man's familiar

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.639
iconography and story beats.

00:06:23.639 --> 00:06:26.880
The final blow, however, came from an entirely
different direction.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.529
Fox Kids, then, quote, "dealing with the realities
of Pokemon as a competitor," didn't have faith

00:06:31.529 --> 00:06:34.839
in Spider-Man Unlimited's ability to take
on Pikachu.

00:06:34.839 --> 00:06:38.990
Thus ended what just might be the weirdest
Spider-Man cartoon of them all, slain by Ash

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:42.589
Ketchum, movie rights, and overworked plotting.

00:06:42.589 --> 00:06:46.990
The Silver Surfer cartoon was a blink-and-you'll-miss
it affair, the sort of footnote even die-hard

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.080
Marvel partisans might not know about.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:54.149
A blend of cel-shading, computer animation,
and Jack Kirby's sensational style, Silver

00:06:54.149 --> 00:06:59.429
Surfer: The Animated Series has only 13 episodes
to its name, but boy, does it throw everything

00:06:59.429 --> 00:07:02.379
it can into those five-ish hours of storytelling.

00:07:02.379 --> 00:07:06.819
Characters like Beta Ray Bill and Uatu the
Watcher populate the show's cosmic confines,

00:07:06.819 --> 00:07:10.999
alongside figures two decades' shy of superstardom,
like Thanos and Gamora.

00:07:10.999 --> 00:07:15.409
It's big, bold science fiction that seeks
to dazzle its viewers, no matter the age,

00:07:15.409 --> 00:07:18.879
with visions of planetary destruction and
galactic altruism.

00:07:18.879 --> 00:07:23.339
Its end came swiftly, however, and the series
languished in obscurity for years.

00:07:23.339 --> 00:07:27.439
Many fans have speculated that the financial
ruin then being faced by Marvel had something

00:07:27.439 --> 00:07:31.499
to do with the cartoon's cancellation, as
the series debuted one year after the company

00:07:31.499 --> 00:07:33.210
filed for bankruptcy.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:37.099
Series creator Larry Brody has gone on the
record as saying Silver Surfer fell apart

00:07:37.099 --> 00:07:41.589
because of a legal dispute between Marvel
and Saban Entertainment, with scant few details

00:07:41.589 --> 00:07:43.580
offered beyond that.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:47.520
A sleek take on the X-canon, Wolverine and
the X-Men is chock-full of the action, angst,

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:50.559
and adventure that fans of Marvel's mutants
love.

00:07:50.559 --> 00:07:54.919
And it took full advantage of the decades
of storytelling it had at its disposal.

00:07:54.919 --> 00:07:58.180
"There's a war coming, and it ain't gonna
be pretty."

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.379
"I agree.

00:07:59.379 --> 00:08:01.020
So, what's next?"

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:04.029
"We bring back the X-Men."

00:08:04.029 --> 00:08:08.300
Characters like Dr. Kavita Rao, the Stepford
Cuckoos, and Marrow made their television

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:12.750
debuts as part of the show, while runs like
Joss Whedon and John Cassaday's Astonishing

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.959
X-Men served as the basis for the plot.

00:08:14.959 --> 00:08:19.349
Though a second season was in production,
it was abruptly scrapped, leaving fans in

00:08:19.349 --> 00:08:20.349
the lurch.

00:08:20.349 --> 00:08:23.770
Corporate shifts had taken place over the
course of the series' run, chief among them

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.319
Disney's purchase of Marvel.

00:08:25.319 --> 00:08:29.461
Fox then held the movie rights to the X-Men,
and as fans would come to know, Marvel was

00:08:29.461 --> 00:08:31.369
building towards cinematic dominance.

00:08:31.369 --> 00:08:36.300
Teams and characters that couldn't contribute
to that effort were automatically of lower

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:40.390
priority, and thus ended Wolverine's time
as the cartoon captain of the X-Men.

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:41.500
The saddest part?

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.500
Head writer Greg Johnson has since revealed
that Deadpool was going to be introduced in

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.900
the cartoon's second season.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:52.750
The DC Animated Universe had gone to outer
space before Green Lantern: The Animated Series

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:55.100
debuted, but never quite to the same degree.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.340
After all, Green Lantern's scope is enormous.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:01.220
The protagonist of the series, Hal Jordan,
is the first human to ever wear the Green

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:02.400
Lantern power ring.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:07.020
He and his friend, Kilowog, a veteran Lantern,
venture into "Frontier Space" together in

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:10.940
the very first episode, a choice that set
the tone for the rest of the series.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:16.200
Fans adored the show's wide-open vantage point,
CG aesthetic, and original characters especially

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:21.140
Razer, a Red Lantern out for redemption who
finds himself falling in love with Aya, an

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:22.140
advanced AI.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:26.440
Despite its passionate fanbase, however, Green
Lantern: The Animated Series was cancelled

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.900
after just one season.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:32.840
Hal Jordan's voice actor, Josh Keaton, spoke
to IGN in the wake of the announcement, acknowledging

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:36.520
fans' anger and the unfortunate cliffhanger
the series now ended on.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:38.510
The reason behind the cancellation?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.250
From what he'd heard, the so-so performance
of the Green Lantern movie meant that a glut

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:47.080
of movie toys ended up confused for animated
series toys, which translated to stores stocking

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.020
less of the latter, depriving the series of
funding.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:53.971
Ryan Reynolds might've managed to bounce back
from Green Lantern's sorry reception, but

00:09:53.971 --> 00:09:58.710
Green Lantern: The Animated Series will remain
a casualty of its failure forever.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:03.360
The Earth's Mightiest Heroes might've premiered
in 2010, but its heart was classic Marvel.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:07.470
Though characters like Captain America, Black
Panther, and Ms. Marvel would eventually join

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:12.650
the team, its debut line-up is the same as
the one from 1963's The Avengers #1: Iron

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:15.420
Man, Ant-Man, Hulk, Thor, and the Wasp.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.820
That doesn't mean it confines itself to one
era of Marvel storytelling, though.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:23.340
Earth's Mightiest Heroes became a beloved
series precisely because it adapted everything

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:28.900
from 2000s comics arcs like "Secret Invasion"
to 1983's beloved "The Ballad of Beta Ray

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:29.900
Bill."

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:34.420
New characters existed seamlessly beside old
ones, while vintage plots were elegantly recalibrated

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:35.570
for younger viewers.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:38.090
It was, in short, a whole heck of a lot of
fun.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:41.890
"They appear to be some kind of man-made,
biological life form."

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:45.590
"You say man-made as if you are proud of this."

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:48.630
So when it wasn't renewed for a third season,
fans were upset.

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:53.250
Earth's Mightiest Heroes was scrapped to clear
the way for a new cartoon, Avengers Assemble,

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:57.760
a change Jeph Loeb, head of Marvel Television,
compared to a change of writer on a comic

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:58.760
series.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.990
Avengers Assemble is technically about the
same characters, but it's also a different

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:05.180
cartoon entirely, far more in line with the
MCU.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:09.510
Though it's fun on its own merits, it's not
Earth's Mightiest Heroes a fact its fans have

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.360
had to get used to.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:16.950
If all X-Men: The Animated Series ever contributed
to the X-Men canon was its killer theme song,

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:18.130
that would've been enough.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:22.690
But it went above and beyond that sick riff
by adapting many of the X-Men's best stories,

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:25.970
from "Days of Future Past" to the infamous
"Dark Phoenix Saga."

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:29.920
A better introduction to these characters
and their world can scarcely be imagined,

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:32.960
and kids responded in kind, watching the show
in droves.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:37.750
X-Men: The Animated Series packed five seasons
full to bursting with time travel, cosmic

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.980
adventure, and societal turmoil.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:43.850
And honestly, its end should've arrived much
earlier than it did, as it'd been plagued

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:48.200
with delays and production errors for years,
and the show's run coincided with an era of

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.190
financial ruin for Marvel that culminated
in their bankruptcy.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:54.670
"Better that we die on our feet than live
on our knees."

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:57.470
But the cartoon's success was undeniable.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:02.110
Despite the fact that the initial series order
had been for 65 episodes, production company

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.770
Saban Entertainment decided to extend the
series to 76 episodes.

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:11.000
In that sense, the series is a true rarity:
It was never really cancelled at all.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.140
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:16.670
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
shows are coming soon.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.560
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

